          ],
          "stoppingConditions": [
            "Stop after the checkpoint is demonstrated and explained; further milestones require fresh evidence and an explicit request."
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "sharedDependencies": [],
  "tradeOffExplanation": "The plan books only one committed integrated activity because the three adopted outcomes are small and naturally belong together in a single report. This keeps the first checkpoint useful and verifiable without cramming later project work into the beginner task. The timebox is 90 minutes with genuine split points at 30 and 60 minutes, and the total effort estimate reflects the work needed to parse, group, detect malformed rows, run a changed example, and check results. Later engineering, tooling, and further project milestones remain strategic and unbooked until the checkpoint is demonstrated and a new request is made."
}

